      "reading_order": 2,
      "needs_vlm": true,
      "extracted_text": "Here is the LaTeX code for the given equation:\n\n```latex\n\\[\nQ = \\frac{h \\times q}{H} = \\frac{8 \\times 60}{8} = 60 \\text{ gallons per minute}.\n\\]\n```\n\nIn this equation:\n- \\( Q \\) represents the flow rate in gallons per minute.\n- \\( h \\) represents some height or head pressure.\n- \\( q \\) represents the quantity or volume.\n- \\( H \\) represents another height or head pressure.\n\nThe calculation shows that when \\( h \\times q = 8 \\times 60 \\), and dividing by \\( H = 8 \\), the result is \\( Q = 60 \\) gallons per minute.",
